# tools/r170_splice.py - R170, 5 patches: followers
# for upper level player characters by class
# (DMG pp.16-18) - the cleric, fighter, ranger,
# thief and assassin recruitment tables, the
# multi-class tables, the Grandfather ladder, the
# arrival timing and the paladin warhorse. A new
# header-only layer, rules/followers.h (the
# grenade.h pattern: the caller rolls the dice
# and builds the rosters).
#
# (1) rules/followers.h: the pp.16-18 print -
#     CLERIC: roll for each of the 7 categories,
#     all 0 level men-at-arms (2-8 heavy cavalry
#     plate mail and shield, lance broad sword
#     mace; 3-12 medium cavalry chain mail and
#     shield, lance flail short sword; 5-30
#     light cavalry studded leather and shield,
#     light crossbow pick; 5-20 heavy infantry
#     splint mail, battle axe long sword; 5-30
#     heavy infantry chain mail, pole arm and
#     hand axe; 5-30 heavy infantry ring mail,
#     heavy crossbow short sword; 10-60 light
#     infantry padded armor and shield, spear
#     club; the pole arm type selected randomly
#     or assigned). FIGHTER: roll once for the
#     leader (01-40 5th level plate mail and
#     shield +2 magic battle axe; 41-75 6th
#     level plate mail and +1 shield, +1 magic
#     spear and +1 dagger; 76-95 6th level +1
#     plate mail and shield, arms as above, a
#     3rd level lieutenant in splint mail and
#     shield with a crossbow of distance; 96-00
#     7th level +1 plate mail and +1 shield, +2
#     magic sword with no special abilities,
#     rides a heavy warhorse with horseshoes of
#     speed) and once for the troops (01-50 20
#     light cavalry ring mail and shield with 3
#     javelins long sword hand axe plus 100
#     heavy infantry scale mail with pole arm
#     and club; 51-75 80 heavy infantry, 20
#     splint mail 60 leather, 20 morning star
#     and hand axe 60 pike and short sword;
#     76-90 60 crossbowmen chain mail, 40 heavy
#     crossbow and short sword 20 light crossbow
#     and military fork; 91-00 60 cavalry, 10
#     banded 20 scale 30 studded leather all
#     with shield, 10 lance bastard sword mace
#     20 lance long sword mace 30 lance and
#     flail). RANGER: 2d12 for the follower
#     count with the d% adjustment ladder (2
#     +25 each roll, 3 +15, 4 +10 first roll
#     only, 5-6 +5 first roll only, 7-9 none,
#     10-12 -5, 13-16 -10, 17-20 -20, 21-24
#     -30; roll again if the result falls in a
#     category no longer permissible or under
#     01), scores over 70 are special, one
#     group only per category. THIEF: 4d6 for
#     the count, the level d% modifier ladder (4
#     +20, 5-6 +15, 7-9 +5, 10-15 none, 16-20
#     -5, 21-24 -10), the category bands (01-50
#     humans table I, 51-70 demi-humans II,
#     71-80 animals III, 81-90 mounts IV, 91-95
#     creatures V, 96-00 special VI); the race
#     of thief (dwarven 01-10, elven 11-20,
#     gnomish 21-25, half-elven 26-30, halfling
#     31-35, half-orcish 36-55, human 56-00);
#     the level of thief (1 on 01-20, 2 on
#     21-45, 3 on 46-65, 4 on 66-80, 5 on
#     81-90, 6 on 91-95, 7 on 96-00); the
#     humans table I (cleric 1-4, druid 2-5,
#     fighter 1-6, ranger 1-3, magic-user 1-3);
#     the demi-humans table II (12 rows: dwarf
#     fighter 1-4 x2, dwarf fighter/thief 1 x1,
#     elf fighter 2-5 x2, elf fighter/magic-user
#     1 x1, elf fighter/magic-user/thief 1 x1,
#     gnome fighter 1-3 x3, gnome
#     fighter/illusionist 1 x1, half-elf
#     cleric/ranger 1 x1, half-elf
#     cleric/fighter/magic-user 1 x1, half-elf
#     fighter/thief 1 x1, halfling fighter 1-3
#     x3, halfling fighter/thief 1 x1); the
#     multi-class thief d6 professions (dwarf
#     fighter; elf fighter 1-3 magic-user 4-5
#     fighter/magic-user 6; gnome fighter 1-5
#     illusionist 6; half-elf same as elf;
#     halfling fighter; half-orc cleric 1-3
#     fighter 4-6) with the note that followers
#     of professed thief class are always
#     neutral good; the animals III (black bear
#     1, brown bear 1, blink dog 2, giant lynx
#     2, giant owl 2), mounts IV (centaur 1-3,
#     hippogriff 1, pegasus 1), creatures V
#     (brownie 1-2, pixie 1-4, pseudo-dragon 1,
#     satyr 1, sprite 2-4) and special creatures
#     VI (copper dragon 1, storm giant 1, treant
#     2-5, werebear 1-2, weretiger 1-2).
#     ASSASSIN: 7d4 for the guild count,
#     adjustable for population; 75 percent
#     desert (as the PHB); newcomers 1st level;
#     the race of assassin (dwarven 01-05,
#     elven 06-10, gnomish 11-15, half-elven
#     16-25, half-orcish 26-50, human 51-00);
#     the level of assassin (1 on 01-15, 2 on
#     16-30, 3 on 31-45, 4 on 46-65, 5 on
#     66-75, 6 on 76-85, 7 on 86-95, 8 on
#     96-00); 1st and 2nd level non-human or
#     part human assassins 25 percent
#     multi-classed, on the multi-classed
#     assassin table (dwarf, elf and half-elf no
#     other class permitted; gnome fighter 1-4
#     illusionist 5-6; half-orc fighter 1-2
#     cleric 3-6). The Grandfather/Grandmother:
#     always 28 followers (1 8th, 2 7th, 3 6th,
#     4 5th, 5 4th, 6 3rd, 7 2nd level) plus 4-16
#     1st level; a displaced leader loses 75
#     percent; the new leader attracts up to 44.
#     Arrival: the first follower appears d10
#     with d6 tens (1-2 +0, 3-4 +10, 5-6 +20)
#     days after the requirements are met, then
#     intervals of 1-8 days; unmet followers wait
#     1-4 days then depart forever; a henchman
#     or servant may receive them. The paladin
#     warhorse: from 4th level, the quest not
#     beyond a 7 days ride, a task of possibly
#     2 or more weeks, the steed possibly wild
#     or guarded by an evil fighter of the same
#     level, then 10 years of service. (2) the
#     regtest include. (3) the R170 audit: every
#     printed cell pinned - CENSUS 88. (4)-(5)
#     the gap report.
#
# JUDGMENTs: (a) the OCR drops the half-orcish
# 26-50 band of the RACE OF ASSASSIN table (the
# print runs dwarven 01-05, elven 06-10,
# gnomish 11-15, half-elven 16-25, half-orcish
# 26-50, human 51-00 - the half-orc is the
# assassin-eligible race the ladder otherwise
# skips); pinned as the print. (b) the OCR
# interleaves the MULTI-CLASSED ASSASSIN table;
# the trailing no-other-class-permitted line
# belongs to the elf row (dwarf, elf and
# half-elf each print no other class permitted),
# confirmed against the print discussions. (c)
# the printed asterisks (race of thief, level
# of thief, race of assassin, level of assassin
# 1 and 2, copper dragon) ride as flags - the
# re-upload OCR shows no footnotes for them.
#
# Idempotent: safe to run twice; a silent run means the
# paste was truncated - this tail ALWAYS prints. An assert
# follows EVERY patch (the R142 lesson). ZERO backslash
# characters in this file; no content string embeds a
# literal apostrophe (the R133b + R147 lessons).
# Commit: "R170: followers by class pinned - the pp.16-18
# recruitment tables, Grandfather ladder and arrival
# timing (census 88)"
import os, sys

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
NL = chr(10)
BS = chr(92)
applied, already, fails = [], [], []

def rd(p):
    with open(os.path.join(ROOT, p), encoding="latin-1") as f:
        return f.read()

def wr(p, s):
    with open(os.path.join(ROOT, p), "w", encoding="latin-1") as f:
        f.write(s)

def patch(p, old, new, tag, marker):
    s = rd(p)
    if marker in s:
        already.append(tag)
        return
    n = s.count(old)
    if n != 1:
        fails.append(tag + ": anchor count " + str(n)
                     + " (expected 1)")
        return
    wr(p, s.replace(old, new))
    applied.append(tag)

def create(p, text, tag, marker):
    fp = os.path.join(ROOT, p)
    if os.path.exists(fp):
        s = rd(p)
        if marker in s:
            already.append(tag)
            return
        fails.append(tag + ": exists without the marker")
        return
    wr(p, text)
    applied.append(tag)

